# Cloudflare / local secrets
.dev.vars*
.env*
.wrangler/
# Node
node_modules/
# OS
.DS_Store

# Scratch probes. Rendering checks and viewport measurements get written into
# tests/ so they can resolve playwright from tests/node_modules, and `git add -A`
# has swept them into a PUBLIC repository three times now. They carry absolute
# paths and no assertions; anything worth keeping becomes a real contract test.
#
# ENUMERATING NAMES IS A LOSING GAME, and the list below is the evidence: it
# caught probe-* and cardshot-* and missed _d2.mjs, which shipped in #18, and
# __chip_probe.html, which was one `--amend` from shipping here. What every one
# of them actually shares is a leading underscore, so that is what is ignored —
# a convention a future probe will follow without this file being updated.
#
# articles/_template/ is the one real leading-underscore path in the tree.
_*
!articles/_template/
!articles/_template/**
tests/*_tmp.mjs
tests/.tmp-*
tests/probe-*.mjs
tests/cardshot-*.mjs

# Scratch directories under tests/. Several suites run the pipeline's own
# emitter into tests/ and clean up in a `finally` — which does not run when a
# suite is killed mid-assertion, and leaves a directory of JSON that `git add
# -A` then offers to commit. The design shots are megabytes of PNG that
# regenerate in two minutes and are pictures of states the payloads already
# describe, so committing them stores a stale copy of something reproducible.
#
# THIS WAS THREE ENUMERATED PATTERNS AND IT MISSED THE FOURTH NAME. `-emit/`,
# `-probe/` and `.shots-*/` did not match `.scratch-track/`, a directory of
# five ad-hoc probe scripts that `git add -A` was ready to commit to a PUBLIC
# repository — which is precisely the failure the underscore rule above was
# written about, recurring one section later in the same file.
#
# So this ignores the SHAPE: a dot-prefixed directory under tests/. No tracked
# path in the repository is one (`git ls-files 'tests/.*'` is empty), the
# suites that create them already use the dot prefix by convention, and a
# future probe directory is caught without this file being updated again.
tests/.*/
